GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com
# 1. Run: ./scripts/setup-oauth.sh    (after gcloud auth login) — creates Android client
# 2. Or manually: console.cloud.google.com → Credentials → Create OAuth client → Android → Package com.draftlock.app → SHA-1 from (keytool -list -v -keystore ~/.android/debug.keystore -alias androiddebugkey -storepass android | grep SHA1) or ./gradlew signingReport → Copy Android Client ID here
# 3. Or paste at runtime: DraftLock → Settings → Advanced Client ID (no rebuild needed) — Android ID required, Web blocks custom scheme
# Current baked fallback is 149732972265-i4i3hi7... (Web) — replace with your new Android ID to fix "Custom scheme not allowed"
